1
00:00:03,742 --> 00:00:06,745
That's the third time you've
been reprimanded in court.

2
00:00:06,832 --> 00:00:09,531
I bent a spoon with my mind.
What's the big deal?

3
00:00:09,618 --> 00:00:11,315
You were testifying
a criminal case.

4
00:00:11,402 --> 00:00:13,578
- You can't be playing tricks.
- It's all theater, right?

5
00:00:13,665 --> 00:00:14,971
Bread and circuses?

6
00:00:15,058 --> 00:00:18,670
Questions, Eve. Right here.

7
00:00:18,757 --> 00:00:20,455
[indistinct shouting]

8
00:00:20,542 --> 00:00:22,283
Eve!

9
00:00:22,370 --> 00:00:24,633
- Eve, a couple of questions.
- 'I'll handle this, Eve.'

10
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:26,809
Ooh. That's Eve Mulberry.
The wine lady?

11
00:00:26,896 --> 00:00:29,942
- 'She grows a great cabernet.'
- What's she accused of?

12
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:32,597
Killing her dance teacher.
They were lovers, I think.

13
00:00:32,684 --> 00:00:33,685
Scandalous.

14
00:00:33,772 --> 00:00:36,079
[cell phone ringing]

15
00:00:36,166 --> 00:00:40,083
I gotta take this. Think about
what you wanna eat. Lisbon.

16
00:00:40,170 --> 00:00:42,651
Deepest sympathies
for Mr. Ruiz's family.

17
00:00:42,738 --> 00:00:44,392
'She's expressed that
on many occasions.'

18
00:00:44,479 --> 00:00:46,394
[male #1]
'Eve, how you
feeling this morning?'

19
00:00:46,481 --> 00:00:48,570
'Are you nervous at all
about closing arguments?'

20
00:00:48,657 --> 00:00:50,006
Wouldn't you be?

21
00:00:50,093 --> 00:00:51,573
Eve's facing
a lifetime in prison

22
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:53,357
'for a crime
she didn't commit.'

23
00:00:53,444 --> 00:00:55,881
Eve, why don't you admit
that you killed Carlos Ruiz?

24
00:00:55,968 --> 00:00:58,797
[male #2]
'Nice try, instead of
going for cheap reaction shots'

25
00:00:58,884 --> 00:01:00,756
'you should be
following my case.'

26
00:01:02,149 --> 00:01:04,542
[indistinct shouting]

27
00:01:29,219 --> 00:01:31,134
CBI. Coming through. CBI.

28
00:01:31,221 --> 00:01:33,223
Eve deserves praise
for her courage.

29
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:37,314
CBI. Eve! CBI. Quick question.
Do you love your mom and dad?

30
00:01:37,401 --> 00:01:39,099
They passed away years ago.

31
00:01:39,186 --> 00:01:41,753
But you think fondly of them.

32
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:43,015
Of course.

33
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,454
Thank you, everyone.

34
00:01:46,541 --> 00:01:48,282
- 'Counsel, one more.'
- 'Eve.'

35
00:01:48,369 --> 00:01:49,500
[male #3]
'Eve!'

36
00:01:58,944 --> 00:02:01,817
Come on.

37
00:02:01,904 --> 00:02:05,212
[Ardiles]
The defense has tried
to paint Eve Mulberry

38
00:02:05,299 --> 00:02:08,476
as sweet as
the grapes she grows

39
00:02:08,563 --> 00:02:10,869
'but you know
the facts of this case.'

40
00:02:10,956 --> 00:02:13,481
[Ardiles]
'You know that
Eve was an adulterer'

41
00:02:13,568 --> 00:02:17,398
even though she may
deny it...and you know

42
00:02:17,485 --> 00:02:21,880
that her lover, Carlos,
blackmailed her for cash

43
00:02:21,967 --> 00:02:26,798
and when Carlos Ruiz went back
to Eve to ask for more money..

44
00:02:26,885 --> 00:02:30,237
...she beat his head into pulp.

45
00:02:30,324 --> 00:02:34,937
Eve silenced her lover to
protect her marketable image.

46
00:02:35,024 --> 00:02:37,505
But this..

47
00:02:37,592 --> 00:02:39,507
...this is the work
of the real Eve.

48
00:02:41,117 --> 00:02:43,598
[Ardiles]
'Take a good, long look..'

49
00:02:43,685 --> 00:02:45,600
'then find her guilty.'

50
00:02:51,519 --> 00:02:53,956
Ardiles. You got a second?

51
00:02:54,043 --> 00:02:55,566
For you, Jane? I got two.

52
00:02:55,653 --> 00:02:58,090
I'll come straight
out with it. You made a mistake.

53
00:02:58,178 --> 00:02:59,875
Eve Mulberry.

54
00:02:59,962 --> 00:03:03,270
- She isn't the killer.
- What are you playing at?

55
00:03:03,357 --> 00:03:05,794
I'm not playing.
I'm just observing.

56
00:03:05,881 --> 00:03:08,318
Eve's nonverbals
are screaming innocence

57
00:03:08,405 --> 00:03:10,581
and sadness for the victim.

58
00:03:10,668 --> 00:03:12,540
Thank you
for the observation.

59
00:03:15,107 --> 00:03:18,589
- She loved her mom and dad too.
- There's more?

60
00:03:18,676 --> 00:03:21,113
Women who murder were abused
by their parents. Not Eve.

61
00:03:21,201 --> 00:03:23,420
When I mentioned them,
she looked to the left

62
00:03:23,507 --> 00:03:25,422
she was tapped
into the brain's left side

63
00:03:25,509 --> 00:03:27,642
where visual
memories are stored.

64
00:03:27,729 --> 00:03:29,470
What if she
looked to the right?

65
00:03:29,557 --> 00:03:31,515
Well, she would've been
accessing her creative mind

66
00:03:31,602 --> 00:03:33,691
to fabricate a story.

67
00:03:33,778 --> 00:03:35,867
This is it?
This is all your evidence?

68
00:03:35,954 --> 00:03:37,695
Well, of course
there's my gut, too

69
00:03:37,782 --> 00:03:40,089
but I didn't think
you'd take thatvery seriously.

70
00:03:40,176 --> 00:03:43,223
That's the first correct
statement you've made.

71
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:45,790
I bet you a million dollars
she's innocent.

72
00:03:45,877 --> 00:03:47,357
If I only had
the money.

73
00:03:47,444 --> 00:03:50,578
[chuckles]
How about a nickel?

74
00:03:50,665 --> 00:03:53,668
Jane, you understand this whole
conversation's pointless, right?

75
00:03:53,755 --> 00:03:56,366
I mean, the jury's started
deliberating. It's over.

76
00:03:56,453 --> 00:03:58,194
Well, the verdict
hasn't been read yet

77
00:03:58,281 --> 00:04:00,414
so technically,
it's still on.

78
00:04:02,894 --> 00:04:04,331
You know, unlike you

79
00:04:04,418 --> 00:04:07,159
Eve Mulberry will not
get away with murder

80
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:09,945
so do us both a favor.
Don't mess with my case.

81
00:04:10,032 --> 00:04:12,295
Oh, I won't mess with it.

82
00:04:12,382 --> 00:04:13,949
I'm gonna fix it.

83
00:04:20,999 --> 00:04:23,393
[theme music]

84
00:04:31,009 --> 00:04:33,011
- There you are. We have to go.
- Where?

85
00:04:33,098 --> 00:04:35,623
We have to talk
to Eve Mulberry. She's innocent.

86
00:04:35,710 --> 00:04:37,581
Well, the jury may
feel differently.

87
00:04:37,668 --> 00:04:40,715
Exactly. That's why we need
to find the real killer.

88
00:04:40,802 --> 00:04:42,412
No. No way.

89
00:04:42,499 --> 00:04:44,240
We don't have time to argue.

90
00:04:44,327 --> 00:04:46,721
- This is not our problem.
- Justice isn't our problem?

91
00:04:46,808 --> 00:04:48,766
The jury has heard arguments
for three months.

92
00:04:48,853 --> 00:04:50,507
They're fully equipped
to determine the truth.

93
00:04:50,594 --> 00:04:52,117
What if they don't?

94
00:04:52,204 --> 00:04:54,424
An innocent woman gets punished
because you were eating.

95
00:04:54,511 --> 00:04:56,121
- Hey, that's my sandwich.
- Mm-hmm?

96
00:04:56,208 --> 00:04:57,340
Give it.

97
00:05:03,912 --> 00:05:06,306
[instrumental music]

98
00:05:20,885 --> 00:05:22,496
Can we help you?

99
00:05:22,583 --> 00:05:25,107
We're with the CBI.
We'd like to talk to you.

100
00:05:25,194 --> 00:05:27,152
No. No. No more police.

101
00:05:27,239 --> 00:05:29,459
These might be my wife's
last hours of freedom.

102
00:05:29,546 --> 00:05:31,592
We plan to spend
them alone. Thank you.

103
00:05:31,679 --> 00:05:34,116
Oh, what if I could offer
a lifetime of freedom?

104
00:05:35,639 --> 00:05:37,206
I know Eve's innocent.

105
00:05:37,293 --> 00:05:40,252
I'd just like
the chance to prove it.

106
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:43,081
I'm sorry, whydo you
want to help me?

107
00:05:43,168 --> 00:05:45,649
Well, let's just say
to whom much is given

108
00:05:45,736 --> 00:05:48,609
much is expected. Yeah.

109
00:05:48,696 --> 00:05:50,959
If you don't mind,
time is a factor here.

110
00:05:51,046 --> 00:05:53,222
Is there somewhere
we can sit down and talk?

111
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:00,316
[Peter]
'I appreciate your
interest in my wife's case'

112
00:06:00,403 --> 00:06:03,450
but what can you possibly do
at this stage of the game?

113
00:06:03,537 --> 00:06:05,539
[Peter]
There's been
hundreds of hours of testimony.

114
00:06:05,626 --> 00:06:08,803
[Jane]
Well, I'll let the courthouse
vultures pick over that carcass.

115
00:06:08,890 --> 00:06:12,023
If I'm gonna help you,
I'm gonna need fresh meat.

116
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:13,764
Why did you take
dance lessons?

117
00:06:13,851 --> 00:06:15,418
Peter's a wonderful dancer.

118
00:06:15,505 --> 00:06:17,377
It was supposed
to be a surprise.

119
00:06:17,464 --> 00:06:19,161
We're both so busy
all the time.

120
00:06:19,248 --> 00:06:20,989
I thought it'd
bring us closer together.

121
00:06:21,076 --> 00:06:23,295
And is that
how you met Carlos Ruiz?

122
00:06:23,383 --> 00:06:25,167
At the dance lessons?

123
00:06:25,254 --> 00:06:26,864
Yeah, that's right.

124
00:06:26,951 --> 00:06:28,823
Ballroom, or, uh, salsa?

125
00:06:28,910 --> 00:06:29,867
Tango.

126
00:06:29,954 --> 00:06:31,129
Ah.

127
00:06:33,088 --> 00:06:34,829
From what I've read
in the newspapers

128
00:06:34,916 --> 00:06:37,527
you spent time with Carlos
outside of just the lessons.

129
00:06:37,614 --> 00:06:39,486
There were
phone calls, meals..

130
00:06:39,573 --> 00:06:41,488
Carlos and I were friends.

131
00:06:41,575 --> 00:06:43,359
A Stanford-educated
winemaker

132
00:06:43,446 --> 00:06:45,622
and a...dance instructor.

133
00:06:45,709 --> 00:06:48,669
Just curious, um,
what'd you talk about?

134
00:06:48,756 --> 00:06:52,281
I don't know. This and that.

135
00:06:52,368 --> 00:06:54,631
You've lied to protect your
husband's feelings, haven't you?

136
00:06:56,111 --> 00:06:58,113
Look at me, Eve.

137
00:06:58,200 --> 00:06:59,941
I know you're feeling
guilt and shame.

138
00:07:00,028 --> 00:07:02,247
I know what this might do
to your marriage

139
00:07:02,334 --> 00:07:05,294
but, uh, the way I see it,
we're your last hope.

140
00:07:05,381 --> 00:07:06,774
You have to trust us.

141
00:07:06,861 --> 00:07:09,298
Honey, w-what is
he talking about?

142
00:07:09,385 --> 00:07:11,387
- Why are you doing this?
- To help you.

143
00:07:11,474 --> 00:07:13,171
You said you believed
I was innocent.

144
00:07:13,258 --> 00:07:14,999
Of murder,
but you weren't hanging out

145
00:07:15,086 --> 00:07:16,784
with your sexy dance teacher

146
00:07:16,871 --> 00:07:19,874
for the stimulating chitchat.
You were attracted to him.

147
00:07:19,961 --> 00:07:22,442
You danced the tango
with the man, for God sakes.

148
00:07:22,529 --> 00:07:24,008
I did not have an affair.

149
00:07:24,095 --> 00:07:25,793
That was a non-contracted
denial.

150
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:28,752
Truth tellers use contractions.
"I didn't have an affair."

151
00:07:28,839 --> 00:07:31,276
This isn't the woman
I saw on the courthouse steps.

152
00:07:31,363 --> 00:07:33,017
I think that you should leave.

153
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:44,072
It's like a band-aid, Eve.

154
00:07:45,726 --> 00:07:47,858
Best to just
tear it off quickly.

155
00:07:54,604 --> 00:07:56,258
It was just a few times.

156
00:07:57,868 --> 00:07:59,435
Are you kidding me?

157
00:07:59,522 --> 00:08:00,828
I'm s..

158
00:08:00,915 --> 00:08:02,220
I'm so sorry.

159
00:08:05,136 --> 00:08:07,095
Peter, you're so busy.
You're always traveling.

160
00:08:07,182 --> 00:08:10,098
- I know that's not an excuse.
- You stay away from me now.

161
00:08:12,796 --> 00:08:14,276
What's going on?

162
00:08:14,363 --> 00:08:17,192
Eve just admitted
to sleeping with Carlos.

163
00:08:17,279 --> 00:08:18,759
Oh.

164
00:08:18,846 --> 00:08:20,151
I'm sorry I missed that.

165
00:08:21,544 --> 00:08:23,328
And sorry,
who are these people?

166
00:08:23,415 --> 00:08:25,809
CBI. They're here to help.

167
00:08:25,896 --> 00:08:28,116
This is my best friend,
my business partner, Amy

168
00:08:28,203 --> 00:08:30,901
and that's
my little sister Gretchen.

169
00:08:30,988 --> 00:08:34,470
What about the blackmail?
You were sleeping with Carlos.

170
00:08:34,557 --> 00:08:36,080
- Did you pay him off?
- 'No.'

171
00:08:36,167 --> 00:08:38,822
He asked for a loan,
but I didn't give it.

172
00:08:38,909 --> 00:08:41,259
- What was the money for?
- A business opportunity.

173
00:08:41,346 --> 00:08:43,087
[Eve]
'I didn't really want to know.'

174
00:08:46,917 --> 00:08:48,832
What are you
still doing here?

175
00:08:48,919 --> 00:08:50,791
I mean,
besides brooding.

176
00:08:53,402 --> 00:08:55,230
Pardon me?

177
00:08:55,317 --> 00:08:58,407
Your wife dropped a bomb on you
and you're still standing.

178
00:08:58,494 --> 00:09:02,106
If it were me, I'd be
out of here by now..

179
00:09:02,193 --> 00:09:05,588
...unless, of course,
I suspected the, uh..

180
00:09:05,675 --> 00:09:07,416
...affair all along.

181
00:09:07,503 --> 00:09:09,592
Why would I hide
my suspicions?

182
00:09:09,679 --> 00:09:11,246
Make yourself look good.

183
00:09:11,333 --> 00:09:12,639
He's right.

184
00:09:12,726 --> 00:09:14,423
If you had knowledge
of the affair

185
00:09:14,510 --> 00:09:16,207
it would make you
a prime suspect.

186
00:09:16,294 --> 00:09:18,775
- I didn't kill anyone.
- You used a contraction.

187
00:09:18,862 --> 00:09:23,475
That's a hopeful sign, but I'll
keep an eye on you and you, Amy.

188
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:26,000
- Me?
- Eve confides in you.

189
00:09:26,087 --> 00:09:28,568
She told you about the affair,
the best friend thing

190
00:09:28,655 --> 00:09:30,744
unlike Gretchen.
She had no idea.

191
00:09:30,831 --> 00:09:33,529
You do have issues with
your sister, though, don't you?

192
00:09:33,616 --> 00:09:35,879
Duh. Like there are sisters
who don'thave issues.

193
00:09:35,966 --> 00:09:37,925
I thought you said
these people were helping.

194
00:09:38,012 --> 00:09:41,537
We are, and I'd say we're off
to a pretty solid start.

195
00:09:41,624 --> 00:09:43,931
I think we need
some time alone.

196
00:09:44,018 --> 00:09:45,410
[Lisbon]
We'll keep in touch.

197
00:09:51,678 --> 00:09:53,114
[Rigsby]
'According to
the court transcript'

198
00:09:53,201 --> 00:09:56,291
there was a cash deposit
for $20,000 paid

199
00:09:56,378 --> 00:09:58,859
into Carlos Ruiz's bank account
the week of his death.

200
00:09:58,946 --> 00:10:01,383
If we're taking Eve's word,
she didn't give him that.

201
00:10:01,470 --> 00:10:03,515
He could've been involved
with something illegal.

202
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:05,300
Peter thought she was
having an affair?

203
00:10:05,387 --> 00:10:07,911
Jane thinks so. It puts him
on the suspect list.

204
00:10:07,998 --> 00:10:09,826
Peter Mulberry runs
a boutique investment firm.

205
00:10:09,913 --> 00:10:11,393
Told the police
he was dinning

206
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:13,221
at his employee's homes
the murder night.

207
00:10:13,308 --> 00:10:15,179
- The employee vouched for him.
- Dig deeper.

208
00:10:15,266 --> 00:10:17,268
Who was the employee?
Do we trust him?

209
00:10:17,355 --> 00:10:18,922
- Her.
- Exactly.

210
00:10:19,009 --> 00:10:21,185
Don't know how we'll
get around the murder weapon.

211
00:10:21,272 --> 00:10:22,709
[Kimball]
'That's a cutter mattock.'

212
00:10:22,796 --> 00:10:24,580
Used for digging trenches
and cutting roots.

213
00:10:24,667 --> 00:10:27,235
It's from Eve's vineyard. Her
fingerprints were all over it.

214
00:10:27,322 --> 00:10:29,803
All this tells me is that
Eve might've been framed.

215
00:10:29,890 --> 00:10:32,588
Make a list of anybody
who held a grudge against her.

216
00:10:32,675 --> 00:10:34,721
Also look back
into Ruiz's phone records.

217
00:10:34,808 --> 00:10:37,201
The original work from the
detectives looks a bit thin.

218
00:10:38,942 --> 00:10:41,597
I know that this isn't
an official case, so thank you.

219
00:10:43,207 --> 00:10:44,948
We're heading
to the crime scene.

220
00:10:45,035 --> 00:10:47,124
Let me know
if you find anything out

221
00:10:47,211 --> 00:10:49,605
and work fast, guys.
The jury's out.

222
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:00,921
[female #1]
'I ain't going anywhere.'

223
00:11:01,008 --> 00:11:03,445
You know what?
Shut up! Get back in the house!

224
00:11:03,532 --> 00:11:05,229
[female #1]
'Don't you walk away!'

225
00:11:05,316 --> 00:11:07,667
[indistinct shouting]

226
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:13,063
Murder was months ago.

227
00:11:13,150 --> 00:11:15,239
What kinda evidence
do you expect to find?

228
00:11:15,326 --> 00:11:17,067
I'll know it when I see it.

229
00:11:17,154 --> 00:11:18,329
Okay.

230
00:11:20,767 --> 00:11:23,160
[intense music]

231
00:11:38,828 --> 00:11:40,482
[knock on door]

232
00:11:40,569 --> 00:11:42,179
[Lisbon]
'CBI. Open up.'

233
00:11:44,399 --> 00:11:46,531
'Hello, police,
open up.'

234
00:11:49,578 --> 00:11:51,101
What do you want?

235
00:11:51,188 --> 00:11:54,017
Uh, w-were you
just watching me?

236
00:11:54,104 --> 00:11:58,848
No, I wasn't.

237
00:11:58,935 --> 00:12:00,023
[knock on door]

238
00:12:02,939 --> 00:12:05,333
Step away from
the door, blondie.

239
00:12:05,420 --> 00:12:07,988
Yeah, easy,
I-I-I'm-I'm with the CBI.

240
00:12:08,075 --> 00:12:10,338
Do you think
I could come in?

241
00:12:18,868 --> 00:12:20,565
"Consultant?"

242
00:12:20,652 --> 00:12:22,872
What makes you think
I'd want a consultant here?

243
00:12:22,959 --> 00:12:25,919
Well, how about a real cop?
I got one across the street.

244
00:12:26,006 --> 00:12:27,355
[knock on door]

245
00:12:27,442 --> 00:12:30,184
She'll be knocking all day.

246
00:12:30,271 --> 00:12:32,186
Go get her.
I'll put on the kettle.

247
00:12:34,405 --> 00:12:35,755
[whistles]
Lisbon!

248
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:41,673
[indistinct chattering]

249
00:12:57,428 --> 00:13:00,823
- Back still hurting, huh?
- I got hit by a car, so yeah.

250
00:13:00,910 --> 00:13:02,869
You should lay off
those pills.

251
00:13:02,956 --> 00:13:04,522
You ever tried yoga?

252
00:13:04,609 --> 00:13:07,047
My neighbor teaches it.
I can get you her number.

253
00:13:07,134 --> 00:13:08,657
[sighs]
No, thanks.

254
00:13:08,744 --> 00:13:10,572
Okay.

255
00:13:10,659 --> 00:13:12,008
Let me know, yeah?

256
00:13:17,144 --> 00:13:18,275
[gunshot]

257
00:13:19,886 --> 00:13:20,843
[gunshot]

258
00:13:20,930 --> 00:13:22,105
Detective Silva?

259
00:13:22,192 --> 00:13:25,195
That's right.

260
00:13:25,282 --> 00:13:27,632
I'm Agent Van Pelt.
This is Agent Rigsby.

261
00:13:27,719 --> 00:13:29,069
We're with the CBI.

262
00:13:29,156 --> 00:13:32,289
Hey. How you doing?
Nice to meet you.

263
00:13:32,376 --> 00:13:34,596
We've been looking
at your files on Eve Mulberry.

264
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:40,341
Oh, yeah?
That was some work, that case.

265
00:13:40,428 --> 00:13:41,864
- Jury come back yet?
- No.

266
00:13:41,951 --> 00:13:43,257
They're still
deliberating.

267
00:13:43,344 --> 00:13:46,216
Eh, no worries.
That loon will get hers.

268
00:13:46,303 --> 00:13:49,524
I love to watch the rich ones
fall, you know what I mean?

269
00:13:49,611 --> 00:13:53,441
We were hoping you could help us
run down some information.

270
00:13:53,528 --> 00:13:55,008
Yeah, sure.
What do you need?

271
00:13:55,095 --> 00:13:56,705
Did you interview
a Conner Reilly?

272
00:13:56,792 --> 00:13:59,751
Records state that Reilly spoke
with Carlos on the murder day.

273
00:13:59,839 --> 00:14:03,538
Reilly...I don't remember.
What does my report say?

274
00:14:03,625 --> 00:14:05,496
There's no notes on him.

275
00:14:05,583 --> 00:14:07,107
Reilly.

276
00:14:07,194 --> 00:14:08,499
Yeah. I remember.

277
00:14:08,586 --> 00:14:10,284
We checked him out.
He looked clean.

278
00:14:10,371 --> 00:14:12,373
Reilly had an alibi
for the murder night?

279
00:14:12,460 --> 00:14:14,418
I guess. I don't recall.

280
00:14:14,505 --> 00:14:17,508
You never talked
to him, did you?

281
00:14:17,595 --> 00:14:19,293
What you getting on me for?

282
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:21,773
We called Reilly.
He didn't call back.

283
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:24,864
We were on Eve Mulberry by then.
Reilly didn't have a record.

284
00:14:24,951 --> 00:14:26,604
No, no record,
no employment history

285
00:14:26,691 --> 00:14:28,432
Facebook page,
not much of anything, really.

286
00:14:28,519 --> 00:14:30,870
We tried calling Reilly but
his phone's been disconnected.

287
00:14:30,957 --> 00:14:33,611
- It's like he never existed.
- What is your issue here?

288
00:14:33,698 --> 00:14:35,309
This case
has already been tried.

289
00:14:35,396 --> 00:14:37,441
We think Eve Mulberry
might be innocent.

290
00:14:37,528 --> 00:14:38,747
Yeah? And why is that?

291
00:14:38,834 --> 00:14:39,879
We have our reasons.

292
00:14:39,966 --> 00:14:41,576
[chuckles]

293
00:14:41,663 --> 00:14:44,492
It's that nut-job psychic
you guys work with, right?

294
00:14:44,579 --> 00:14:46,886
Janet or Jane.

295
00:14:46,973 --> 00:14:50,019
- He's showboating again, right?
- I feel sorry for you guys.

296
00:14:50,106 --> 00:14:52,543
You're like, uh,
stooges in a comedy act.

297
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:54,328
- Yeah, he's not a psychic.
- Yeah, whatever.

298
00:14:54,415 --> 00:14:55,895
Do you have
anything on Reilly?

299
00:14:55,982 --> 00:14:58,158
Anything at all
that might help us find him?

300
00:14:58,245 --> 00:15:00,029
Oh, let me think.

301
00:15:00,116 --> 00:15:02,858
No. Sorry.

302
00:15:02,945 --> 00:15:05,165
- Hey!
- Hey! I'm sorry.

303
00:15:11,649 --> 00:15:14,261
[Lisbon]
'So you're home here
a lot, Mrs. Williams?'

304
00:15:14,348 --> 00:15:17,307
[Williams]
'I am retired,
so, yes, I am.'

305
00:15:17,394 --> 00:15:19,309
[Lisbon]
And, um..

306
00:15:19,396 --> 00:15:21,833
were you home the night
that your neighbor was murdered?

307
00:15:25,663 --> 00:15:27,927
I can see you've
lived here a long time

308
00:15:28,014 --> 00:15:30,233
and you like to
keep an eye on things.

309
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:33,933
- Tell us what you saw.
- What are you doing over there?

310
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:36,631
- Admiring your lovely home.
- Oh.

311
00:15:36,718 --> 00:15:39,112
Do you have help keeping,
uh, things so tidy?

312
00:15:39,199 --> 00:15:43,203
No, I do not.
Do I look like an invalid?

313
00:15:43,290 --> 00:15:45,640
Gloria. Why don't you
tell us what you saw?

314
00:15:45,727 --> 00:15:47,947
I'll tell you what
I told the other police

315
00:15:48,034 --> 00:15:50,732
stomping through my house.
I saw nothing.

316
00:15:50,819 --> 00:15:53,082
- Okay, Lisbon. Let's go.
- I'm not done.

317
00:15:53,169 --> 00:15:55,128
She's won't talk.
Look at her. She's scared.

318
00:15:55,215 --> 00:15:57,652
That's why she hides
behind the curtains all day.

319
00:15:57,739 --> 00:16:00,916
I'm not hiding from anyone.
I keep vigil over my house.

320
00:16:01,003 --> 00:16:02,744
Well, there's no shame
in being afraid.

321
00:16:02,831 --> 00:16:05,007
Old age can be
a terrifying time of life.

322
00:16:05,094 --> 00:16:06,791
You're right. We should go.

323
00:16:06,878 --> 00:16:10,056
Yes, thank you very much for
your time, ma'am. Thank you.

324
00:16:10,143 --> 00:16:11,579
I saw someone.

325
00:16:11,666 --> 00:16:13,102
-Oh.
- Ooh.

326
00:16:13,189 --> 00:16:16,540
I saw, uh, a woman
the night that Mexican..

327
00:16:16,627 --> 00:16:18,890
The Latino boy was murdered.

328
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:22,111
She went into the house, and
then minutes later, she ran out.

329
00:16:22,198 --> 00:16:24,200
Can you describe her?

330
00:16:24,287 --> 00:16:28,030
She had a tote bag.
She was slim build.

331
00:16:28,117 --> 00:16:30,032
She had blonde hair,
long blonde hair.

332
00:16:32,208 --> 00:16:34,558
She look like this?
Eve mulberry?

333
00:16:34,645 --> 00:16:37,170
Yes, that's her.
Exactly. So there.

334
00:16:47,615 --> 00:16:50,313
We can't quit now. I don't care
what the neighbor said.

335
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:52,489
An eyewitness identified
Eve as the killer.

336
00:16:52,576 --> 00:16:54,535
Did you see a single
working clock there?

337
00:16:54,622 --> 00:16:56,145
A wristwatch,
an alarm, anything?

338
00:16:56,232 --> 00:16:57,799
No. So?

339
00:16:57,886 --> 00:17:00,628
She lives cooped up here
with no sense of the time.

340
00:17:00,715 --> 00:17:03,761
She probably confused the night
of the murder with another one.

341
00:17:03,848 --> 00:17:05,328
So you're saying
she's flat-out wrong?

342
00:17:05,415 --> 00:17:07,026
I'm just saying
Eve is innocent.

343
00:17:07,113 --> 00:17:09,289
I need evidence to
keep the team on this.

344
00:17:09,376 --> 00:17:10,638
We got a lead.

345
00:17:10,725 --> 00:17:13,075
The victim talked
to a Conner Reilly

346
00:17:13,162 --> 00:17:15,338
but Reilly was using
a phony social security number.

347
00:17:15,425 --> 00:17:16,644
- It's an alias.
- Who for?

348
00:17:16,731 --> 00:17:18,298
This guy. Terry Murphy.

349
00:17:18,385 --> 00:17:21,388
He came over on a tourist visa
two years ago from Ireland.

350
00:17:21,475 --> 00:17:23,651
[Rigsby]
'He's a tech scammer, internet
fraud, identity creation.'

351
00:17:23,738 --> 00:17:25,435
He's violent.
He's been a murder suspect.

352
00:17:25,522 --> 00:17:27,176
Ask, and you shall receive.

353
00:17:27,263 --> 00:17:28,917
One of our CIs
has contacts there.

354
00:17:29,004 --> 00:17:30,527
She's asking around now.

355
00:17:32,747 --> 00:17:35,967
- Okay. We keep working.
- We should talk to Eve again.

356
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:38,274
Maybe she knows what was
going on with Murphy.

357
00:17:38,361 --> 00:17:40,755
- Maybe.
- You're the boss on this one.

358
00:17:40,842 --> 00:17:42,931
- Okay, don't be like that.
- Like what?

359
00:17:43,018 --> 00:17:44,367
It's what you want.

360
00:17:44,454 --> 00:17:47,022
What I want
is a little smile.

361
00:17:47,109 --> 00:17:51,679
Well, you can't
have everything.

362
00:17:51,766 --> 00:17:53,768
I checked out
the employee that was dining

363
00:17:53,855 --> 00:17:56,162
with the husband
on the murder night.

364
00:17:56,249 --> 00:17:58,164
And after the wife's
murder trial started

365
00:17:58,251 --> 00:18:00,427
Peter Mulberry gave
the woman a huge promotion.

366
00:18:00,514 --> 00:18:02,646
Suddenly she's
the company's youngest V.P.

367
00:18:02,733 --> 00:18:05,301
- He bribed her for the alibi?
- Maybe. I'll keep digging.

368
00:18:05,388 --> 00:18:06,520
Alright.

369
00:18:13,657 --> 00:18:14,832
Summer. Welcome back.

370
00:18:16,443 --> 00:18:18,358
I'm not gonna say
that I'm thebest

371
00:18:18,445 --> 00:18:20,273
confidential informant ever

372
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:22,579
but I am pretty
high up on the list.

373
00:18:22,666 --> 00:18:23,885
What do you have?

374
00:18:23,972 --> 00:18:25,800
This girl
I used to hustle with..

375
00:18:25,887 --> 00:18:29,064
...she's now into identify
theft. She knows Murphy.

376
00:18:29,151 --> 00:18:31,110
I said that I had
some stolen information

377
00:18:31,197 --> 00:18:33,155
to sell
and she made a call.

378
00:18:33,242 --> 00:18:36,376
- Can she set up a meet?
- Already done.

379
00:18:36,463 --> 00:18:39,118
Murphy will be at the Grafton
Street tavern in an hour.

380
00:18:43,034 --> 00:18:44,993
Is it me,
or do you look impressed?

381
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:47,778
No, it's just you. We'll have
Summer wait at the bar.

382
00:18:47,865 --> 00:18:49,606
When Murphy arrives,
we'll scoop him up.

383
00:18:49,693 --> 00:18:52,827
If Summer gets Murphy to make an
offer that'd give us leverage.

384
00:18:52,914 --> 00:18:55,221
I could do that.

385
00:18:55,308 --> 00:18:56,787
It'll cost you extra.

386
00:18:56,874 --> 00:18:59,529
All we have to do
is fit her with a wire.

387
00:19:02,358 --> 00:19:03,707
Okay.

388
00:19:03,794 --> 00:19:05,535
Just get him
to make the offer.

389
00:19:05,622 --> 00:19:08,625
Excuse yourself to the bathroom.
That's it. Then we move in.

390
00:19:08,712 --> 00:19:10,671
Okay.

391
00:19:10,758 --> 00:19:13,195
Make the deal, hit the can.
Done and done.

392
00:19:13,282 --> 00:19:16,633
That'll be $500,
$800 if I make the case.

393
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:18,200
I'll wire you up.

394
00:19:33,650 --> 00:19:35,086
You again?

395
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:37,088
Uh, we're looking for Eve.

396
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:38,916
She just took
a walk with Amy

397
00:19:39,003 --> 00:19:40,831
you might wanna
give her a minute.

398
00:19:40,918 --> 00:19:43,182
Eve and Peter just had
an epic throw-down.

399
00:19:43,269 --> 00:19:46,010
The waterworks
were ridiculous.

400
00:19:46,097 --> 00:19:49,144
Okay. Well, you think
I can sample the goods?

401
00:19:49,231 --> 00:19:50,363
Yeah, sure.

402
00:19:57,065 --> 00:19:59,328
That is our new cab.

403
00:19:59,415 --> 00:20:01,243
New to the business?

404
00:20:01,330 --> 00:20:02,984
Is it that obvious?

405
00:20:03,071 --> 00:20:05,595
You poured red wine
in a white wine glass.

406
00:20:05,682 --> 00:20:07,118
Oh, well.

407
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:09,860
Yeah, I'm just helping out
here during the trial.

408
00:20:09,947 --> 00:20:11,906
You don't own
a piece of the action?

409
00:20:11,993 --> 00:20:16,606
Uh, no. The wine company belongs
to my sister and her BFF.

410
00:20:16,693 --> 00:20:18,478
And who owns
the private villa?

411
00:20:18,565 --> 00:20:21,785
Eve won that jackpot
when she married Peter.

412
00:20:21,872 --> 00:20:24,527
All the land
belongs to him, so..

413
00:20:24,614 --> 00:20:26,790
Gretchen,
that glass is wrong.

414
00:20:26,877 --> 00:20:28,531
Your shoes are wrong

415
00:20:28,618 --> 00:20:30,533
'but you don't see me
complaining about it.'

416
00:20:30,620 --> 00:20:32,274
We've talked about this.

417
00:20:32,361 --> 00:20:35,930
There's a reason investors
are knocking down the door.

418
00:20:36,017 --> 00:20:38,106
It's an attention to detail.

419
00:20:38,193 --> 00:20:41,892
Thank you. You haven't
taken any of the offers?

420
00:20:41,979 --> 00:20:44,025
We go back
and forth about it.

421
00:20:44,112 --> 00:20:46,114
From a business standpoint,
it makes sense.

422
00:20:46,201 --> 00:20:49,335
But we don't want to be one of
those giant corporate vineyards

423
00:20:49,422 --> 00:20:51,902
because then it wouldn't
be about the wine.

424
00:20:51,989 --> 00:20:55,297
Yes, it's beautifully earthy,
with, uh..

425
00:20:55,384 --> 00:20:57,212
...a hint of acid.

426
00:20:57,299 --> 00:20:59,823
Do you notice
the tobacco note at the end?

427
00:20:59,910 --> 00:21:02,826
- The cab's my favorite.
- Ah, yes. Mmm.

428
00:21:02,913 --> 00:21:05,742
I'm sorry, could we speak
to Eve alone for a moment?

429
00:21:05,829 --> 00:21:07,048
Gretchen, let's go.

430
00:21:07,135 --> 00:21:08,267
Gladly.

431
00:21:12,314 --> 00:21:14,273
Do you recognize this man?

432
00:21:15,839 --> 00:21:17,493
No.

433
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:19,147
[Eve]
'Should I?'

434
00:21:19,234 --> 00:21:21,976
His name's Terry Murphy.
He's a known criminal.

435
00:21:22,063 --> 00:21:25,109
Carlos was in touch with him
the day of his murder.

436
00:21:25,196 --> 00:21:27,068
Oh, my,
what kind of criminal?

437
00:21:27,155 --> 00:21:28,809
[Lisbon]
'He's into
identity theft mostly'

438
00:21:28,896 --> 00:21:32,247
but he's also done some illegal
surveillance and wiretapping.

439
00:21:32,334 --> 00:21:34,728
What did Carlos have
to do with him?

440
00:21:34,815 --> 00:21:36,730
Well, we were hoping
you'd tell us.

441
00:21:36,817 --> 00:21:40,560
I wish I could, but this is good
news, right? This could help us.

442
00:21:40,647 --> 00:21:43,780
I feel like the jury's gonna
walk outta that room any minute.

443
00:21:43,867 --> 00:21:45,652
We're doing
everything we can.

444
00:21:45,739 --> 00:21:47,915
Yeah. Very good. Thank you.

445
00:21:51,527 --> 00:21:53,747
Do you realize,
every single time I deal

446
00:21:53,834 --> 00:21:56,184
with your people,
things go to hell?

447
00:21:56,271 --> 00:21:58,969
Osvaldo. Come in. Sit down.

448
00:21:59,056 --> 00:22:02,277
Is there something in the water
here? I need to know.

449
00:22:02,364 --> 00:22:04,627
I need to know
why your team is interfering

450
00:22:04,714 --> 00:22:06,803
with a state murder trial.

451
00:22:06,890 --> 00:22:08,762
I understand your anger.

452
00:22:08,849 --> 00:22:10,633
No, you don't.

453
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:12,505
The state has spent
millions of dollars

454
00:22:12,592 --> 00:22:14,028
not to mention
thousands of man-hours

455
00:22:14,115 --> 00:22:15,638
prosecuting this case.

456
00:22:15,725 --> 00:22:18,815
- And yet evidence was missed.
- What evidence?

457
00:22:18,902 --> 00:22:21,252
The victim was in contact
with a violent criminal

458
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,994
the day of his murder.
That doesn't concern you?

459
00:22:24,081 --> 00:22:25,474
No.

460
00:22:25,561 --> 00:22:27,520
No, that's the concern
of an appeals court

461
00:22:27,607 --> 00:22:30,349
if Mrs. Mulberry believes
that her due process was denied.

462
00:22:30,436 --> 00:22:34,048
An appeals court. How long will
she have to spend in prison?

463
00:22:34,135 --> 00:22:36,050
If she's innocent,
she deserves our help.

464
00:22:38,269 --> 00:22:41,272
You want to know
why Jane took this case?

465
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:44,232
Because Eve loved her parents.

466
00:22:44,319 --> 00:22:46,190
That's crazy, right?

467
00:22:46,277 --> 00:22:48,236
I thought there was
something in the water

468
00:22:48,323 --> 00:22:50,804
but I can see
the problem now.

469
00:22:50,891 --> 00:22:52,022
It's you.

470
00:23:02,772 --> 00:23:05,166
[rock music]

471
00:23:08,604 --> 00:23:11,651
Testing, testing, one, two.
Kimball Cho's a wallaby.

472
00:23:28,885 --> 00:23:30,017
[Kimball]
'Here's Murphy.'

473
00:23:36,937 --> 00:23:38,068
[male #4]
'Beer?'

474
00:23:42,246 --> 00:23:43,639
Summer, is it?

475
00:23:43,726 --> 00:23:44,858
It is.

476
00:23:47,295 --> 00:23:50,603
What do you got for me, girly?

477
00:23:50,690 --> 00:23:52,605
A long list of numbers.

478
00:23:52,692 --> 00:23:55,129
Social security, credit cards,
driver's license.

479
00:23:55,216 --> 00:23:58,349
- About a hundred of each.
- Where do you get 'em?

480
00:23:58,437 --> 00:24:01,048
Clients, the kinds
with high credit limits.

481
00:24:01,135 --> 00:24:04,312
Won't know it hits them
till it's too late.

482
00:24:04,399 --> 00:24:06,445
What sort of business you in?

483
00:24:06,532 --> 00:24:09,273
[Summer]
'I'm a working girl.'

484
00:24:09,360 --> 00:24:10,927
[Murphy chuckles]

485
00:24:11,014 --> 00:24:12,189
Bang on.

486
00:24:14,365 --> 00:24:17,020
You know, a little of your
honey would sweeten the pot.

487
00:24:19,327 --> 00:24:20,763
$5,000 for the information.

488
00:24:20,850 --> 00:24:23,505
Are you touched? Not here.

489
00:24:31,208 --> 00:24:33,080
Wait. Let it play out.

490
00:24:44,961 --> 00:24:47,268
Five thousand ain't gonna
happen, sunshine.

491
00:24:47,355 --> 00:24:49,792
You'll get three.
That's the rate.

492
00:24:49,879 --> 00:24:51,446
That's it. Let's move.

493
00:24:54,014 --> 00:24:57,060
[Summer]
'How do I know I can trust you?'

494
00:24:57,147 --> 00:25:00,237
[Murphy]
'You're questioning me?'

495
00:25:00,324 --> 00:25:04,198
My name is my word.
Ask anyone I do business with.

496
00:25:04,285 --> 00:25:07,331
Some friends of mine said that
you worked with Carlos Ruiz.

497
00:25:07,418 --> 00:25:11,335
I'd ask him about you,
but...he's dead.

498
00:25:11,422 --> 00:25:14,338
She's trying to make our case.

499
00:25:14,425 --> 00:25:16,036
[Murphy]
'Well, now..'

500
00:25:16,123 --> 00:25:18,517
You've got spirit,
I'll give you that.

501
00:25:18,604 --> 00:25:22,042
[sighs]
You think so?
I was trying to act tough.

502
00:25:22,129 --> 00:25:23,696
You never know
in these situations.

503
00:25:23,783 --> 00:25:26,002
[both chuckle]

504
00:25:26,089 --> 00:25:28,048
So what's the deal
with Carlos?

505
00:25:28,135 --> 00:25:30,006
- Carlos?
- Yeah.

506
00:25:30,093 --> 00:25:33,227
He had some plan to install
ATM skimmers in strip clubs.

507
00:25:33,314 --> 00:25:34,881
Nice enough plan..

508
00:25:34,968 --> 00:25:37,927
...got me to invest
20 grand in it..

509
00:25:38,014 --> 00:25:41,104
Which he then spent
on strippers and booze.

510
00:25:41,191 --> 00:25:43,454
So what'd you do?

511
00:25:43,542 --> 00:25:44,847
What did Ido?

512
00:25:44,934 --> 00:25:47,154
- Let's go.
- Just give her a minute.

513
00:25:47,241 --> 00:25:48,808
[Summer]
'Yeah.'

514
00:25:48,895 --> 00:25:51,288
'You didn't just let him
steal from you, did you?'

515
00:25:54,422 --> 00:25:55,641
[gasps]

516
00:25:55,728 --> 00:25:58,644
What's that to do
with you? Hmm?

517
00:25:58,731 --> 00:26:00,602
Let go.

518
00:26:00,689 --> 00:26:03,257
Where's that
list of numbers?

519
00:26:03,344 --> 00:26:06,826
- Stop it.
- I want to see it now.

520
00:26:06,913 --> 00:26:07,870
[door thuds]

521
00:26:07,957 --> 00:26:10,003
Police! Don't move!

522
00:26:12,179 --> 00:26:13,572
[both grunt]

523
00:26:13,659 --> 00:26:14,790
[Kimball]
Hey!

524
00:26:19,578 --> 00:26:22,015
[Rigsby]
'Give me your hands.
Hands behind your back.'

525
00:26:22,102 --> 00:26:23,233
You alright?

526
00:26:28,282 --> 00:26:30,240
You owe me $800.

527
00:26:32,721 --> 00:26:33,853
Come on.

528
00:26:39,032 --> 00:26:40,424
So a jury's deliberating
this case as we speak

529
00:26:40,511 --> 00:26:42,513
and the $20,000
in Ruiz's bank account

530
00:26:42,601 --> 00:26:45,429
is a key piece of evidence,
you gave it to him.

531
00:26:45,516 --> 00:26:48,128
That's right. So what?

532
00:26:48,215 --> 00:26:51,697
So I think you killed Carlos
because he lost your money.

533
00:26:51,784 --> 00:26:53,437
That would be foolish.

534
00:26:53,524 --> 00:26:57,659
If I killed him, I wouldn't
get it back, now, would I?

535
00:26:57,746 --> 00:27:00,706
Don't mind me. Rigsby,
I brought you a cup of tea.

536
00:27:00,793 --> 00:27:02,882
Uh, no, I'm good.
Thank you.

537
00:27:02,969 --> 00:27:06,102
Oh. No good deed
goes unpunished. Uh, you?

538
00:27:14,067 --> 00:27:16,025
Yous both seem
like agreeable men.

539
00:27:19,420 --> 00:27:21,640
Can't we find a reasonable
solution to this problem?

540
00:27:21,727 --> 00:27:23,903
Something that's
beneficial to all of us?

541
00:27:23,990 --> 00:27:27,123
- He's trying to bribe us.
- Yeah, sounds like it to me.

542
00:27:27,210 --> 00:27:30,997
Your words,
not mine...but..

543
00:27:31,084 --> 00:27:32,738
...now you come to mention it..

544
00:27:32,825 --> 00:27:35,305
...I do believe that everyone
has their price point.

545
00:27:37,090 --> 00:27:39,483
What are you willing to pay?

546
00:27:39,570 --> 00:27:42,573
If I'm out within the hour,
five grand to each of ya.

547
00:27:42,661 --> 00:27:45,098
You killed a man.
You're not bribing your way out.

548
00:27:45,185 --> 00:27:47,143
Certainly not
for 5 grand, anyhow.

549
00:27:47,230 --> 00:27:50,059
I killed no man.

550
00:27:50,146 --> 00:27:52,235
I deal in information,
not murder.

551
00:27:52,322 --> 00:27:56,283
Yes, fake IDs, right?
Um..

552
00:27:56,370 --> 00:27:58,764
How do the, uh,
fake identity things work?

553
00:27:58,851 --> 00:28:01,114
- I always wanted to know.
- I'll explain it later.

554
00:28:01,201 --> 00:28:03,986
Could you explain it now?
I mean, he's not gonna talk.

555
00:28:04,073 --> 00:28:07,381
I understand it's a matter of
making a phony credit profile.

556
00:28:07,468 --> 00:28:08,774
- 'That's all?'
- 'Yeah, that's all.'

557
00:28:08,861 --> 00:28:10,645
If you were a hack,
that's all.

558
00:28:10,732 --> 00:28:14,736
Well, what if you're not a hack?
How do you go about it then?

559
00:28:14,823 --> 00:28:17,217
Huh? Theoretically speaking.

560
00:28:21,438 --> 00:28:27,270
True identity farming is an art
that takes decades to set up.

561
00:28:27,357 --> 00:28:29,490
You invent children.

562
00:28:29,577 --> 00:28:31,492
Set up bank accounts
for them

563
00:28:31,579 --> 00:28:34,974
file tax returns,
register them as voters

564
00:28:35,061 --> 00:28:39,674
and then, years later,
you have the perfect identities

565
00:28:39,761 --> 00:28:43,765
ready and waiting
for real people to step into.

566
00:28:43,852 --> 00:28:45,419
That's it?

567
00:28:45,506 --> 00:28:47,203
There's a cd
full of personal information

568
00:28:47,290 --> 00:28:50,511
you have to fill out
first, but, uh..

569
00:28:50,598 --> 00:28:51,686
Yeah, that's it.

570
00:28:53,557 --> 00:28:58,606
And how much would one charge
for this, uh, particular..

571
00:28:58,693 --> 00:29:01,304
'...thing? Theoretically.'

572
00:29:01,391 --> 00:29:04,307
Well, now, we're talking
top of the line here.

573
00:29:04,394 --> 00:29:06,135
Mm-hmm.

574
00:29:06,222 --> 00:29:08,616
Two hundred thousand
for a brand-new you.

575
00:29:08,703 --> 00:29:10,879
I'll get back to the
interrogation, if that's okay?

576
00:29:10,966 --> 00:29:13,360
Yeah, by all means.

577
00:29:13,447 --> 00:29:17,016
[Lisbon]
'Alright.
Thanks for the heads-up.'

578
00:29:17,103 --> 00:29:19,496
Bad news. That was
a friend from the courthouse.

579
00:29:19,583 --> 00:29:22,456
The jury didn't order dinner.
They're closing in on a verdict.

580
00:29:22,543 --> 00:29:25,198
Hmm. We need to hustle.

581
00:29:25,285 --> 00:29:28,375
Call Eve, have her come in
tell her you wanna update her.

582
00:29:28,462 --> 00:29:31,030
- I'm springing Murphy.
- No. He's our prime suspect.

583
00:29:31,117 --> 00:29:32,988
He didn't kill Carlos,
that doesn't mean

584
00:29:33,075 --> 00:29:35,034
he can't be useful to us.
Uh...yeah.

585
00:29:35,121 --> 00:29:37,297
Video surveillance equipment.
Those little cameras?

586
00:29:37,384 --> 00:29:39,865
- I'm gonna need a few.
- Mind telling me one thing?

587
00:29:39,952 --> 00:29:40,953
Like what I'm planning?

588
00:29:41,040 --> 00:29:42,476
Yeah, that would be super.

589
00:29:42,563 --> 00:29:43,651
[chuckles]

590
00:29:43,738 --> 00:29:44,870
No?

591
00:29:47,350 --> 00:29:49,396
You're annoyed
I didn't stick to the agenda

592
00:29:49,483 --> 00:29:52,921
but all's well that
ends well. We're a team.

593
00:29:53,008 --> 00:29:55,184
Stuff happens,
and, uh, we move on.

594
00:30:03,323 --> 00:30:05,542
[sighs]
We're not a team.

595
00:30:05,629 --> 00:30:07,414
Sign that.

596
00:30:07,501 --> 00:30:09,590
Here's your final payment.

597
00:30:09,677 --> 00:30:11,157
"Final payment?"

598
00:30:11,244 --> 00:30:13,812
You were reckless and put
everyone in danger today.

599
00:30:13,899 --> 00:30:16,075
If I can't trust you,
I can't use you.

600
00:30:18,991 --> 00:30:21,297
So what, that's it?
You're done with me?

601
00:30:22,908 --> 00:30:24,039
Yes.

602
00:30:33,832 --> 00:30:36,704
Oh, you're back
for more, are you?

603
00:30:36,791 --> 00:30:39,533
Do me a favor
and get us another cup of cha

604
00:30:39,620 --> 00:30:41,883
with a bit of sugar
in it this time.

605
00:30:41,970 --> 00:30:45,191
Get it yourself.
I pulled in a favor.

606
00:30:45,278 --> 00:30:46,845
You're a free man..

607
00:30:46,932 --> 00:30:48,847
...under one condition.

608
00:30:51,371 --> 00:30:53,329
I need a new identity.

609
00:30:58,378 --> 00:30:59,945
Do you, now?

610
00:31:00,032 --> 00:31:02,512
Well, you wanted to know
my price point. That's it.

611
00:31:02,599 --> 00:31:04,340
And I expect
a friends-and-family discount

612
00:31:04,427 --> 00:31:06,647
from your usual fee.

613
00:31:06,734 --> 00:31:08,867
How do I know
this isn't entrapment?

614
00:31:08,954 --> 00:31:11,870
You don't, but try this.

615
00:31:11,957 --> 00:31:14,524
You get me a new identity
or I'll book you

616
00:31:14,611 --> 00:31:17,310
for receiving
stolen information.

617
00:31:17,397 --> 00:31:20,269
That should be enough to get you
extradited back to Ireland

618
00:31:20,356 --> 00:31:23,272
where you're wanted in
connection with two homicides..

619
00:31:23,359 --> 00:31:25,231
...or is that three?

620
00:31:30,062 --> 00:31:32,281
I'll do it for $100,000.

621
00:31:33,935 --> 00:31:37,112
Okay, I'm in a tight spot.
How quickly can you work?

622
00:31:37,199 --> 00:31:39,158
How quick can you
fill out the forms?

623
00:31:39,245 --> 00:31:41,377
The cd, right.
When do I get that?

624
00:31:41,464 --> 00:31:43,075
One hour.

625
00:31:43,162 --> 00:31:46,165
There's a parking lot at
the south end of Fourth Street.

626
00:31:46,252 --> 00:31:49,559
I'll meet you at the bottom
with the cd, but..

627
00:31:49,646 --> 00:31:52,562
'...I'll need a deposit
to get me started.'

628
00:31:52,649 --> 00:31:53,824
'Ten thousand.'

629
00:31:55,696 --> 00:31:57,654
I'll send a courier.

630
00:32:05,880 --> 00:32:07,621
As long as they've the cash.

631
00:32:07,708 --> 00:32:09,231
Just don't be late.

632
00:32:11,538 --> 00:32:12,669
[indistinct chattering]

633
00:32:14,541 --> 00:32:16,673
- We're gonna have a contest.
- For what?

634
00:32:16,760 --> 00:32:18,458
See who has
the best Irish accent.

635
00:32:18,545 --> 00:32:22,679
Rigsby, you're up first.
Don't argue. We don't have time.

636
00:32:22,766 --> 00:32:26,335
[clears throat]
I, um..

637
00:32:26,422 --> 00:32:28,033
[Irish accent]
My name's Wayne Rigsby.

638
00:32:28,120 --> 00:32:31,166
Why I'm talking with
an Irish accent right now, I..

639
00:32:31,253 --> 00:32:33,473
...don't really know.

640
00:32:33,560 --> 00:32:36,737
Uh, okay. Cho?

641
00:32:36,824 --> 00:32:38,391
- No.
- Oh, come on.

642
00:32:38,478 --> 00:32:40,654
We know you have
all sorts of hidden talents.

643
00:32:42,786 --> 00:32:44,571
Rigsby it is, then.

644
00:32:44,658 --> 00:32:46,399
Uh, practice learning this.

645
00:32:52,579 --> 00:32:54,494
- Did you get those cameras?
- Yeah.

646
00:32:56,235 --> 00:32:57,758
Good man. Thank you.

647
00:33:00,804 --> 00:33:03,198
How are you two holding up?

648
00:33:03,285 --> 00:33:04,808
Things have been better.

649
00:33:04,895 --> 00:33:08,377
Lisbon, look at these.

650
00:33:08,464 --> 00:33:10,162
What are those?

651
00:33:11,990 --> 00:33:13,774
Wireless surveillance cameras.

652
00:33:13,861 --> 00:33:16,429
The new owner of Carlos' house
was replastering the ceiling.

653
00:33:16,516 --> 00:33:17,778
He found 'em
hidden everywhere.

654
00:33:17,865 --> 00:33:19,301
Murphy was
a surveillance expert.

655
00:33:19,388 --> 00:33:21,260
And Carlos owed
Murphy lots of money.

656
00:33:21,347 --> 00:33:24,785
Well, maybe Murphy installed
the cameras to keep tabs on him.

657
00:33:24,872 --> 00:33:27,483
Not "maybe."
We traced the serial numbers.

658
00:33:27,570 --> 00:33:30,356
They were bought by one of
Murphy's established aliases.

659
00:33:30,443 --> 00:33:33,228
If those were in the ceiling, it
could've recorded the murders.

660
00:33:33,315 --> 00:33:35,404
Murphy might have
evidence on the real killer.

661
00:33:35,491 --> 00:33:37,841
- It's possible.
- A bit of a long shot, right?

662
00:33:37,928 --> 00:33:39,582
I'd say it's our only shot.

663
00:33:39,669 --> 00:33:42,150
We just released Murphy.
I'm gonna bring him back in.

664
00:33:42,237 --> 00:33:44,761
Yeah, I'm sorry.
You're gonna have to leave now.

665
00:33:44,848 --> 00:33:47,155
- Of course. Thank you so much.
- Yeah, thank you.

666
00:33:51,246 --> 00:33:53,074
- Well done.
- I try.

667
00:33:56,556 --> 00:33:59,124
[Irish accent]
"Listen. Listen.
Do not interrupt."

668
00:33:59,211 --> 00:34:00,777
Ready?

669
00:34:00,864 --> 00:34:02,214
No, not really.

670
00:34:02,301 --> 00:34:04,477
You go to war
with the army you have.

671
00:34:04,564 --> 00:34:06,087
Read what's there,
and hang up.

672
00:34:06,174 --> 00:34:07,610
Okay.

673
00:34:07,697 --> 00:34:10,135
[Irish accent]
"Listen. Do not interrupt.

674
00:34:10,222 --> 00:34:13,747
"I know who killed Carlos Ruiz,
and I've a video to prove it.

675
00:34:13,834 --> 00:34:16,576
"for $10,000, I'll give you
this video on a cd.

676
00:34:16,663 --> 00:34:19,361
"There's a parking lot at
the south end of Fourth Street.

677
00:34:19,448 --> 00:34:21,624
- I'll be waiting for you in.."
- Forty five minutes.

678
00:34:21,711 --> 00:34:24,323
Forty five minutes.
Don't be late.

679
00:34:24,410 --> 00:34:26,716
- Bravo.
- The jury reached a verdict.

680
00:34:26,803 --> 00:34:28,979
- When are they reading it?
- Six o'clock.

681
00:34:29,067 --> 00:34:31,156
- Almost an hour. Shall we?
- Yeah.

682
00:34:44,691 --> 00:34:46,475
It's been 45 minutes.

683
00:34:46,562 --> 00:34:48,738
44.

684
00:34:48,825 --> 00:34:50,000
Patience.

685
00:34:56,877 --> 00:34:58,052
[tires screeching]

686
00:35:00,620 --> 00:35:01,795
Hello.

687
00:35:10,978 --> 00:35:13,111
[Lisbon]
'Okay, Murphy's here.'

688
00:35:22,555 --> 00:35:24,513
Where are you?

689
00:35:26,167 --> 00:35:27,299
[tires screeching]

690
00:35:46,405 --> 00:35:47,362
[car door closes]

691
00:35:47,449 --> 00:35:49,016
Hello.

692
00:35:49,103 --> 00:35:50,452
Where's the money?

693
00:35:50,539 --> 00:35:52,411
Ten thousand dollars.
It's all there.

694
00:35:57,720 --> 00:35:59,113
Now the cd?

695
00:36:07,774 --> 00:36:09,210
Where else
is the video stored?

696
00:36:09,297 --> 00:36:11,473
Take it easy now.

697
00:36:11,560 --> 00:36:13,954
Where else
is the video stored?

698
00:36:14,041 --> 00:36:15,564
W-what video?

699
00:36:15,651 --> 00:36:18,828
The video on the cd.
The video of the murder!

700
00:36:18,915 --> 00:36:20,352
Where else is it stored?

701
00:36:20,439 --> 00:36:23,485
What video? What murder?
You off your nut?

702
00:36:23,572 --> 00:36:24,965
Amy. Put the gun down.

703
00:36:25,052 --> 00:36:26,706
No, no. No, no.

704
00:36:26,793 --> 00:36:27,794
Drop it!

705
00:36:27,881 --> 00:36:29,970
- Now!
- You called me!

706
00:36:30,057 --> 00:36:31,798
I-I know there's a video.

707
00:36:31,885 --> 00:36:35,454
The cops told Eve there's a
murder video. I spoke to her.

708
00:36:35,541 --> 00:36:39,458
I didn't call ya. There's no
video on there, you silly cow.

709
00:36:41,895 --> 00:36:43,940
Okay, come on.
Let's make this snappy.

710
00:36:44,027 --> 00:36:45,812
We got eight minutes to 6:00.

711
00:36:45,899 --> 00:36:48,118
- You set all this up?
- Who set what up?

712
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:50,947
- What the hell's going on?
- Amy killed Carlos.

713
00:36:51,034 --> 00:36:53,733
She thought your cd had
a video of the murder.

714
00:36:53,820 --> 00:36:55,300
Bring Murphy
into the station

715
00:36:55,387 --> 00:36:57,215
and book him for receiving
stolen information.

716
00:36:57,302 --> 00:36:59,086
I'm taking Amy to court.

717
00:36:59,173 --> 00:37:00,218
Seven minutes.

718
00:37:04,178 --> 00:37:07,268
In the matter ofCalifornia
against Eve Mulberry

719
00:37:07,355 --> 00:37:10,228
all rise for the honorable
Judge Isley Markman.

720
00:37:14,493 --> 00:37:17,757
The jury's reached a verdict.
Bailiff, please bring them in.

721
00:37:17,844 --> 00:37:19,628
- Hold on!
- 'What is going on there?'

722
00:37:19,715 --> 00:37:21,108
Bailiff, remove those people.

723
00:37:21,195 --> 00:37:23,937
Wait. We're with the CBI.

724
00:37:24,024 --> 00:37:26,461
I know who you are.

725
00:37:26,548 --> 00:37:28,028
He pulled
that mind reading trick

726
00:37:28,115 --> 00:37:29,464
in my courtroom last month.

727
00:37:29,551 --> 00:37:31,031
[Lisbon]
'I'm sorry to barge in'

728
00:37:31,118 --> 00:37:33,816
but this is the woman
who killed Carlos Ruiz.

729
00:37:33,903 --> 00:37:35,644
[Ardiles]
'They're showing contempt
for these proceedings.'

730
00:37:35,731 --> 00:37:38,125
- This is an embarrassment.
- It's an embarrassment to you.

731
00:37:38,212 --> 00:37:41,998
You had no idea
Amy framed Eve for murder.

732
00:37:42,085 --> 00:37:44,305
Amy?

733
00:37:44,392 --> 00:37:46,873
If you did this,
you have to say something now.

734
00:37:48,788 --> 00:37:50,224
I want a lawyer first.

735
00:37:50,311 --> 00:37:51,660
Enough.

736
00:37:51,747 --> 00:37:54,402
Everyone in
my chambers now, except you.

737
00:38:02,367 --> 00:38:05,021
My client is willing
to confess

738
00:38:05,108 --> 00:38:06,806
but under one condition..

739
00:38:06,893 --> 00:38:10,288
...the D.A.'s office takes
the death penalty off the table.

740
00:38:10,375 --> 00:38:12,681
Well?

741
00:38:12,768 --> 00:38:15,249
How did Jane know
that it was a frame job?

742
00:38:15,336 --> 00:38:17,686
The neighbor saw a woman
with long blonde hair

743
00:38:17,773 --> 00:38:19,949
leaving the victim's house
the night of the murder.

744
00:38:20,036 --> 00:38:21,516
Jane knew that
Eve was innocent.

745
00:38:21,603 --> 00:38:24,040
It had to have been
a woman in a wig.

746
00:38:24,127 --> 00:38:26,173
Eve's sister, she couldn't
have pulled this off.

747
00:38:26,260 --> 00:38:28,828
[Lisbon]
'She couldn't even
pour a glass of wine.'

748
00:38:28,915 --> 00:38:32,092
'Amy was the only one
who was capable and had motive.'

749
00:38:34,094 --> 00:38:36,226
Unbelievable.

750
00:38:36,314 --> 00:38:38,316
Yeah. Death is off the table.

751
00:38:39,752 --> 00:38:41,275
Start talking, young lady.

752
00:38:44,365 --> 00:38:47,107
I just wanted
what was mine, you know?

753
00:38:49,501 --> 00:38:53,896
Our wine is a sensation.
Everybody loves it.

754
00:38:53,983 --> 00:38:55,594
Investors wanted
to jump on board

755
00:38:55,681 --> 00:38:57,683
and they wanted
to make us rich.

756
00:38:59,554 --> 00:39:02,427
And Eve wants to stay small.

757
00:39:02,514 --> 00:39:05,212
Small? She has acres of land.
She has a rich husband.

758
00:39:05,299 --> 00:39:07,083
What does she know about that?

759
00:39:07,170 --> 00:39:09,129
I work nearly
a hundred hours a week.

760
00:39:09,216 --> 00:39:12,262
I can barely make my mortgage.

761
00:39:12,350 --> 00:39:15,135
[Amy]
'I thought this was my shot.'

762
00:39:15,222 --> 00:39:18,225
And Eve had told you
about her affair with Carlos.

763
00:39:18,312 --> 00:39:21,489
You knew, if he was killed,
she'd be investigated.

764
00:39:21,576 --> 00:39:23,622
Yes.

765
00:39:23,709 --> 00:39:26,842
I told Carlos
I was a friend of Eve's.

766
00:39:26,929 --> 00:39:29,628
[Amy narrating]
I didn't know if someone
would see me so..

767
00:39:29,715 --> 00:39:33,240
...I wore the wig
to make them think I was Eve.

768
00:39:33,327 --> 00:39:36,939
I said I was interested
in taking dance lessons.

769
00:39:37,026 --> 00:39:38,506
He invited me in.

770
00:39:47,689 --> 00:39:51,214
And the murder weapon,
I took from our vineyard

771
00:39:51,301 --> 00:39:53,347
I knew her fingerprints
would be on it.

772
00:39:56,655 --> 00:39:57,786
[glass shattering]

773
00:40:20,853 --> 00:40:22,376
What are you doing here?

774
00:40:24,204 --> 00:40:26,162
I want my job back.

775
00:40:26,249 --> 00:40:28,251
[dings]
Go home.

776
00:40:28,338 --> 00:40:30,079
You know,
I was handling that situation

777
00:40:30,166 --> 00:40:33,039
just fine today
until you busted in.

778
00:40:33,126 --> 00:40:36,346
I need this job, Kimball.
I've given up everything else.

779
00:40:36,434 --> 00:40:37,609
[elevator whirring]

780
00:40:37,696 --> 00:40:40,568
Why would you
take this from me?

781
00:40:40,655 --> 00:40:42,352
[paper rustles]

782
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:45,181
- Because you're crazy!
- What are you gonna do, huh?

783
00:40:45,268 --> 00:40:47,445
- Hit me?
- No. That's what you want.

784
00:40:47,532 --> 00:40:49,316
What?

785
00:40:49,403 --> 00:40:51,144
That's why you kept
pushing Murphy today.

786
00:40:51,231 --> 00:40:54,887
- What are you talking about?
- You get off on danger.

787
00:40:54,974 --> 00:40:58,281
It provides a distraction
from your unhappy life!

788
00:40:58,368 --> 00:41:00,632
Screw you, Kimball!

789
00:41:00,719 --> 00:41:02,851
Y-you're not so difficult
to figure out yourself!

790
00:41:02,938 --> 00:41:05,941
Yeah? What'd you
figure out?

791
00:41:06,028 --> 00:41:09,249
Nothing! And it's
driving me crazy!

792
00:41:09,336 --> 00:41:10,772
- Who are you?
- I gotta go.

793
00:41:10,859 --> 00:41:12,774
No! No. No. No.

794
00:41:12,861 --> 00:41:15,429
- Only if you give me my job.
- Move.

795
00:41:15,516 --> 00:41:17,475
You fired me
because you like me.

796
00:41:17,562 --> 00:41:20,173
You like me,
and don't know what to do.

797
00:41:20,260 --> 00:41:21,827
- Admit it!
- Okay, I like you.

798
00:41:21,914 --> 00:41:24,351
Admit it!

799
00:41:24,438 --> 00:41:26,484
Oh.

800
00:41:26,571 --> 00:41:28,529
I'm so sorry. Y-you do?

801
00:41:31,010 --> 00:41:33,491
Can I go now?

802
00:41:33,578 --> 00:41:37,277
[sighs]

803
00:41:37,364 --> 00:41:38,496
Mmm.

804
00:41:49,550 --> 00:41:52,466
[male #5]
'Were you astonished
by the verdict?'

805
00:41:52,553 --> 00:41:54,990
[female #2]
'Eve, this way.'

806
00:41:55,077 --> 00:41:57,471
[indistinct shouting]

807
00:42:02,432 --> 00:42:04,783
[male #6]
'How about
a kiss for the cameras?'

808
00:42:07,220 --> 00:42:08,917
[clapping]

809
00:42:09,004 --> 00:42:10,179
Jane.

810
00:42:11,354 --> 00:42:12,530
Your nickel.

811
00:42:14,488 --> 00:42:17,012
Bet you're glad
you didn't bet a million.

812
00:42:17,099 --> 00:42:18,231
Goodnight, Jane.

813
00:42:22,278 --> 00:42:24,629
[shouting continues]

814
00:42:37,511 --> 00:42:39,905
[theme music]

